# the release tag, so this file has neither and needs no bump per release. The concept DOI
# is added once Zenodo has archived the first release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mj_viser: MuJoCo in the browser, live, as plans, and replayed"
message: "If you use mj_viser in your work, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Siddhartha
    family-names: Srinivasa
    email: siddhartha.srinivasa@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5091-106X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/personalrobotics/mj_viser"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - robotics
  - mujoco
  - visualization
  - simulation
  - viser
abstract: >
  mj_viser renders MuJoCo simulations in the browser, on Viser. It is read-only and
  caller-driven: it shows the state its caller supplies and never steps a simulation or
  commands a robot. It follows running simulations live, with named channels, camera
  images, and contacts; previews planned motions as per-browser ghosts; records states as
  native Viser recordings; and, through an optional ssrobot integration, follows ssrobot
  runs and replays their verified run bundles.
